course: dictionary
lesson: 13375
title: A name for people and a language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names. A name for a people, a place or a person starts with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence. «Hausa» is one of these words. It is not an English word, so you will not find it in most English stories.
explain: «The Hausa are a large people of West Africa.» Here Hausa is a noun. It names a group of people, mainly in northern Nigeria and Niger. The clue is the word people: Hausa tells you who they are.
explain: «She speaks Hausa at home and English at school.» Now Hausa names a language. The clues are speaks, at home and at school, because a language is something you speak. Ask yourself: is this word a people, a place or a thing?
fact: «Hausa» is a name, so it always begins with a capital letter.
fact: The Hausa are a large people of West Africa, mainly in northern Nigeria and Niger.
fact: The Hausa language is spoken by tens of millions of people, as a first or second language.
fact: «Hausa» can also describe things, as in «Hausa traders» or «the Hausa language».
fact: Kano is a Hausa city with old walls and dye pits.
exercise: «The Hausa are a large people of West Africa.» What kind of word is Hausa here? | A type of food | A colour | A sport | *A name for a people
exercise: «She speaks Hausa at home.» What does Hausa name here? | A large river | A market in Kano | A dye pit | *The Hausa language
exercise: «Many Hausa traders sell cloth in the market.» Why does Hausa start with a capital letter? | Because it is an English verb | *Because it is a name | Because it is a long word | Because it is always the first word
test: «Hausa traders sold cloth in the busy market.» What does Hausa describe here? | A kind of food | *Traders from the Hausa people | Traders who sell cloth from Scotland | Old walls of a city
test: «Millions of people speak Hausa in West Africa.» What is Hausa in this sentence? | *The language spoken by many people in West Africa | A kind of cloth | The name of a football team | A colour in the flag of Nigeria
exam: «Hausa is not an English word, but it is used in lessons about Africa.» What is true? | It is a city in Scotland | It is a verb meaning to run | It is a colour | *It names a people and their language
